# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Private overlay.
#
# Everything that is ours-only lives under private/ and is backed up to the
# Citra-AI repo. One directory rather than a curated pattern list, because
# patterns are what kept going wrong: `*.ps1` and `.env*` both match files this
# repo legitimately ships (.env.example, Citra-UI/install-and-run.ps1,
# Citra-Service/scripts/update_milvus_schema.ps1 — 22 of them), so a glob-based
# rule silently removes needed files. A single directory cannot.
private/

# Firebase hosting publishes citra-ai.com. That is OUR deployment, not
# something a self-hoster runs, and .firebaserc names the live projects. These
# three were tracked here until 2026-08-17; they now live in private/Citra-UI/.
Citra-UI/.firebaserc
Citra-UI/firebase.json
Citra-UI/deploy-simple.ps1

# Android signing material. Stays at these paths because gradle reads them
# there, so it cannot move under private/.
**/debug.keystore
Citra-UI/keystore-info.txt
Citra-UI/sha1.txt

# AWS deployment. These publish to OUR EC2 estate via SSM and name the
# instances (Citra-AI-1, citra-ai-test-1, ...). Deployment to our infrastructure
# is not something a self-hoster runs; local deployment is shared and stays.
**/deploy.sh
**/deploy.yml
**/DEPLOY-CHECKLIST.md
**/docker-compose.aws.yml
